Z||000000||Homicidal||05-04-2000||03:01 PM||||Okay, as I said in my other post, the my car is acting odd.<P>I started it this morning, started with some trouble, and I got lots of ewhite exhaust.  Plus some water.  I assume morning condensation.<P>But after I got out of school the car had a slow "RRRRRRRRRR" sound, like if your battery was dead, before starting.  I turned it off, tried again and got the same thing.<P>I get home, I let it sit for about 1 minute, I start it, and it starts PERFECTLY!  ???<P>Why is this happening?  What would cause this?||||reg||8
Z||000001||Homicidal||05-04-2000||03:08 PM||||One last update:<P>I started it and my music started skipping and my radio started turning off and on when I started it!<P>Is it me, or does sound like a bad battery?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||bad88||05-06-2000||12:49 AM||||could be an electrical short too or the voltage regulator.  My guess would be the radio for a short but first check the battery voltage with a voltmeter with engine off then running, it should increase with engine running (alternator working) you should have at least 12 volts with just the battery and at least 13 with alternator running, other wise check for a grounded wire.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Racer 1||05-06-2000||01:50 AM||||Time to get a priest and some holy water!||||reg||4
Z||000004||Phaeton||05-06-2000||06:16 AM||||Just got here from your previous post, this is great, more questions!<P>Radio's have low voltage cutoffs, but the ignition switch on the steering column also shuts off accessories while starting. Does the key return crisply to the run positon or ease back smoothly like its on shock absorbers?<P>Any chance of borrowing a volt meter to probe the cranking voltage and systems voltage fluctuations immediately after start? Cold readings and hot reading?<P>How about a companion to start the Fiero while you stick your head way way way into the engine compartment? sputtering? hissing? squeaks? grating? movement or lack thereof? smoke? smells? vibrations? shifts in karma?<P>Sure am glad its not my head and hands in there!  Oh, and do it hot also, just to have a baseline of proper function.<P>  TTFN||||reg||12
Z||000005||Brian84SE||05-06-2000||08:58 AM||||How old is the battery?  If it is 3+ years old, change it anyway. It'll be the best $50 spent.  This will not only help to rule out other problems but will give you years of reliable service. Ever start sweating when it's 10 degrees out and you know your battery is old and you can't be late for work???||||reg||1
Z||000006||Brian84SE||05-06-2000||09:01 AM||||If you just bought the car and you dont know the history of the battery, change it.  A tow truck to come and give you a jump will cost at least the cost of the battery.||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||05-06-2000||04:21 PM||||Just take the battery to a parts store and have it load-tested.  It's free.  ||||reg||1
